          <TR> 
            <TD><font size="3"><b>
<FONT SIZE=7 COLOR=BLUE> 
			<br>
	
When you don't get your NEW LEGS 
			<br>
	
AKA When EQ makes you nutty! 
			<br>
	
</font> 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
So there I was heading to the Plane of Hate.. one of my favorite spots. But NOPE!!!!! Real life just had to intervene! 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
Seems as though one of our clients decided he did not want to pay for our services.... there I am sitting in the office.. everyone is staring at me.... I am grimacing... sweet thoughts of wreaking havoc are going south... I issue this proclamation " But he has to pay". 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
Ummmm nope he refused. 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
Sweet thoughts of new gold legs.... not to be.. but I am Ok i can fix this problem. 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
Ummm nope I could not. 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
So I end up with all this guys belongings.... and I miss the Hate raid as I exhaust myself with many failed attempts to get the Plat <errrr cash>. 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
Two greaves fall.... TWO! Grats to Shoshannah and Luie!!! 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
Death to the customer!!!  
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
Today the Idiot < I mean the customer> suddenly has the money. But its too late...  I did not get my legs. There is no way in Hades this guy is not paying for this affront... after all I am still wearing Blue legs! Grrrrrrrr! 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
So what does an angry bard do? He creates a fictitous storage fee of $100 and made him pay that too! Then Mr. CEO calls and asks " Why did you charge him $100 more?". To which I responded "BECAUSE!" Would have been rather hard to explain all about my blue legs and how I should have gold legs and had I missed out on green legs it would have been $500. Hell I am sure the CEO got a cut of it anyway...darn CEO's. 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
So for those who say this is just a game I sayyyyyyyyy.... PFFFFFT! 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
Oh yeah did I say grats to Brother Luie and the Lovely Shosh? 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
Moral of the story... The customer is not only rarely right, but the customer just generally SuXXors! Wait thats not right the moral is " Don't Mess with a fashionably challenged BARD!" Ahh well you can all make your own moral:) 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
This was a theraputic session from the Slacker Bard of Brell. 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
/looks around for his lounge chair 
			<br>
	
/realizes he threw it out the window last night in a fate of rage 
			<br>
	
/ snickers 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	

</b></font></TD>
