        <TABLE align=center width=80%>
          <TR> 
            <TD><b><font size=4>06/28/2001</font></b> </TD>
          </TR>
          <TR> 
            <TD><font size="3"><b>
<font size=10 color=green> 
			<br>
	
Uber attempt fails in a large SPLAT! 
			<br>
	
</font> 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
Last night the brave warriors with help from some friends began to explore the "HOLE". After many intense battles we managed to secure 20ft of new turf!  
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
Well actually we just slaughtered lots of stuff. 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
In an attempt to be Uber it was determined that with the right speed and trajectory it would be possible to land directly on top of Master Yaelthingy causing massive amounts of damage the likes of which the Master could not withstand. It was determined that the bard must do it due to the uber speed factor! 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
Initially the jump went as planned.. a perfect rate of speed allowed for a hasty decent directly at Master Yael's head. The happy screams of the bard could be heard as he drifted off into the dark depths.  
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
However, something went drastically wrong. 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
The last thing anyone heard was the happy screams abruptly cut off by a wet splatting sound, followed by the sounds of contented ratmen happily chewing on some fresh bones. 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
In other words some dumb bard fell in the hole and pretty much ended our good raid!!! Darn Bards! 
			<br>
	
 
			<br>
	
See you all Monday. 
</b></font></TD>
          </TR>
